  "description": "WebWeave 2026 is an exciting offline web development challenge that provides participants with an opportunity to demonstrate their knowledge of web technologies, creativity, and problem-solving skills. The event challenges students to design and develop a functional web page based on a theme revealed during the contest . The event begins with a Prelims round consisting of 20 MCQs covering HTML, CSS, JavaScript, and scripting libraries . The prelims test participants' fundamental concepts and practical understanding of web technologies and will be conducted separately for internal and external participants. Qualified participants will advance to the Main Round , where they will have 2 hours to create a web page based on the given theme . Participants must work independently without internet access or AI tools, demonstrating their own technical skills and creativity. WebWeave encourages participants to transform their ideas into functional, visually appealing, and user-friendly digital experiences while applying their knowledge of modern web development. Venue: MCA Lab Date: 9th October 2026 Team Size: 1–2 members Eligibility: B.Tech / MCA / M.Tech WebWeave 2026 — Weave Your Code, Shape Your Web.",
