    "details": "<div class=\"flex max-w-full flex-col gap-4 [&amp;&gt;div:has([data-free-thinking-preview-answer=true])+:is(.text-message,.relative:has(&gt;.text-message))]:-mt-2 grow\">\n<div class=\"min-h-8 text-message relative flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 text-start break-words whitespace-normal outline-none keyboard-focused:focus-ring [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-1\" dir=\"auto\" tabindex=\"0\" data-message-author-role=\"assistant\" data-message-id=\"f6840601-039d-4f1a-be7d-f1c9feeb7b9a\" data-message-model-slug=\"gpt-5-6\" data-turn-start-message=\"true\">\n<div class=\"flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden\">\n<div class=\"fbskMG_root LR5Y_W_content markdown prose dark:prose-invert wrap-break-word w-full light markdown-new-styling\">\n<p dir=\"auto\" data-start=\"53\" data-end=\"386\"><strong data-start=\"53\" data-end=\"70\">WebWeave 2026</strong> is an exciting <strong data-start=\"86\" data-end=\"123\">offline web development challenge</strong> that provides participants with an opportunity to demonstrate their knowledge of web technologies, creativity, and problem-solving skills. The event challenges students to design and develop a functional web page based on a <strong data-start=\"348\" data-end=\"385\">theme revealed during the contest</strong>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\" data-start=\"388\" data-end=\"685\">The event begins with a <strong data-start=\"412\" data-end=\"429\">Prelims round</strong> consisting of 20 MCQs covering <strong data-start=\"461\" data-end=\"511\">HTML, CSS, JavaScript, and scripting libraries</strong>. The prelims test participants' fundamental concepts and practical understanding of web technologies and will be conducted separately for internal and external participants.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\" data-start=\"687\" data-end=\"956\">Qualified participants will advance to the <strong data-start=\"730\" data-end=\"744\">Main Round</strong>, where they will have <strong data-start=\"767\" data-end=\"824\">2 hours to create a web page based on the given theme</strong>. Participants must work independently without internet access or AI tools, demonstrating their own technical skills and creativity.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\" data-start=\"958\" data-end=\"1152\">WebWeave encourages participants to transform their ideas into <strong data-start=\"1021\" data-end=\"1094\">functional, visually appealing, and user-friendly digital experiences</strong> while applying their knowledge of modern web development.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\" data-start=\"1154\" data-end=\"1273\"><strong data-start=\"1154\" data-end=\"1164\">Venue:</strong> MCA Lab<br data-start=\"1172\" data-end=\"1175\" /><strong data-start=\"1175\" data-end=\"1184\">Date:</strong> 9th October 2026<br data-start=\"1201\" data-end=\"1204\" /><strong data-start=\"1204\" data-end=\"1218\">Team Size:</strong> 1&ndash;2 members<br data-start=\"1230\" data-end=\"1233\" /><strong data-start=\"1233\" data-end=\"1249\">Eligibility:</strong> B.Tech / MCA / M.Tech</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\" data-start=\"1275\" data-end=\"1327\" data-is-last-node=\"\" data-is-only-node=\"\"><strong data-start=\"1275\" data-end=\"1327\" data-is-last-node=\"\">WebWeave 2026 &mdash; Weave Your Code, Shape Your Web.</strong></p>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>",
